<title>SINGAPORE: Inno-Pacific Holdings losses deepen.</title>
<headline>Inno-Pacific Holdings losses deepen.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net loss			     12.77   vs     4.39 (loss)</p>
<p>    Group shr (cents) (loss)	  5.00   vs     2.00 (loss)</p>
<p>    Turnover			     70.65   vs   182.00</p>
<p>    Other income incl. interest     1.78   vs     1.92</p>
<p>    Interest (expense)		  4.00   vs     3.95</p>
<p>    Depreciation (expense)	    5.84   vs     3.17</p>
<p>    Loss from associates		0.95   vs     0.60 (loss)</p>
<p>    Pre-tax loss			 18.57   vs     2.55 (loss)</p>
<p>    Tax				     0.25   vs     1.44</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries		     3.71   vs     0.30</p>
<p>Note - Inno-Pacific Holdings Ltd, in the business of paper and food trading, said group turnover for the year fell 61.2 percent to S$70.6 million compared to 1995 due mostly to the divestment of the paper group IFP on July 1, 1996.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
